  "causal_chain": [
    "FPDFPage_GenerateContent -> CPDF_PageContentGenerator::GenerateContent -> UpdateContentStreams -> CPDF_PageContentManager constructor",
    "CPDF_PageContentManager unconditionally initializes objects_with_multi_refs_ with GetObjectsWithMultipleReferences(document_) before adding the new signature content stream",
    "GenerateContent then calls UpdateResourcesDict, which can repeat the same global traversal",
    "IsPageResourceShared for an indirect resource dictionary -> GetObjectsWithMultipleReferences",
    "CloneResourcesDictEntries with indirect ExtGState/Font/XObject entries can also call GetObjectsWithMultipleReferences",
    "ObjectTreeTraverser follows reachable references using GetDirect -> GetOrParseIndirectObjectInternal; caches parsed indirect objects in document",
    "Closing a page does not evict this document object cache",
    "InitNewObjNumOffsets includes cached valid objects in incremental; WriteNewObjs serializes them without per-object dirty filtering"
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "This proves a source-level amplification mechanism, not the exact object inventory or repeated bytes of the unavailable real PDFs.",
    "Reachable objects are not necessarily all xref entries; orphan/unreachable objects need not be loaded.",
    "Stream object materialization does not imply eager decoding of all payload bytes.",
    "Resource clones preserve indirect references; dictionary cloning alone does not prove image payload duplication.",
    "Page graphical object counts differ from indirect document object counts."
